<title>NORWAY: Aker completes west African oil unit.</title>
<headline>Aker completes west African oil unit.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian engineering and offshore company Aker ASA said on Wednesday Aker Marine in Texas had completed installation of the anchoring systems of the production ship on Mobil's Zafiro field off Equatorial Guinea in west Africa.</p>
<p>The Zafiro Producer, lying in 200 metres of water, is a converted 286,000 dwt tanker equipped with processing facilities, with a capacity of up to 80,000 barrels per day.</p>
<p>The vessel is the second largest tanker to have been converted for production, the company said in its weekly Aker Pulse newsletter.</p>
<p>&quot;A number of fields worldwide are under consideration for development with such units -- both newbuildings or conversions,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
